## CI/CD Local Checks (After Major Changes)
After any major change, perform these local checks similar to CI/CD:

### 1. Code Quality Checks (Fix Issues Found)
```bash
# Run all linting and formatting checks - FIX ISSUES AUTOMATICALLY
poetry run ruff check eshop/ --fix --unsafe-fixes
poetry run ruff format eshop/
poetry run black eshop/
poetry run mypy eshop/ --ignore-missing-imports
poetry run bandit -r eshop/

# IMPORTANT: Fix remaining MyPy errors manually before proceeding
# Target: 0 MyPy errors, minimal Ruff warnings
```

### 2. Testing
```bash
# Run all tests
poetry run pytest tests/ -v --cov=eshop --cov-report=html
poetry run pytest tests/ -v --cov=eshop --cov-report=term-missing
```

### 3. Manual Testing (Quick Start & Stop)
```bash
# Start the application in background
poetry run uvicorn eshop.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 &
APP_PID=$!

# Wait for startup
sleep 3

# Test health endpoints quickly
curl -s http://localhost:8000/health | python -c "import sys, json; print('✅ Health OK' if json.load(sys.stdin).get('status') == 'ok' else '❌ Health failed')"
curl -s http://localhost:8000/api/v1/health | head -1
curl -s http://localhost:8000/health/detailed | head -1

# Stop app
kill $APP_PID 2>/dev/null || true
```

### 4. Health Checks
- Verify all health endpoints return 200 OK
- Check database connectivity
- Verify Redis connection
- Test RabbitMQ connectivity
- Validate Keycloak integration

### 5. Setup Scripts Validation
```bash
# Test setup scripts
./setup-dev.sh
./setup-docker.sh
./setup-podman.sh
./setup-keycloak.sh
```

### 6. Container Testing
```bash
# Test Docker
docker-compose up --build -d
docker-compose ps
docker-compose logs app
docker-compose down

# Test Podman (if available)
podman-compose up --build -d
podman-compose ps
podman-compose logs app
podman-compose down
```

### 7. Documentation Updates
- Update README.md with any new features/changes
- Verify all setup instructions work
- Update API documentation if endpoints changed
- Check environment variable documentation

### 8. Pre-commit Checks
```bash
# Run pre-commit hooks
poetry run pre-commit run --all-files
```

### 9. Final Validation
- [ ] All linting checks pass
- [ ] All tests pass with good coverage
- [ ] Application starts without errors
- [ ] Health checks return healthy status
- [ ] Setup scripts work correctly
- [ ] Docker/Podman containers start successfully
- [ ] README is up to date
- [ ] No breaking changes introduced

### 10. Git Commit Guidelines
After all checks pass, commit with short, descriptive messages:

```bash
# Format: <type>: <short description>
git add .
git commit -m "feat: migrate to fastapi-keycloak"
git commit -m "fix: resolve pylance errors in auth module"
git commit -m "docs: update setup instructions"
git commit -m "refactor: improve error handling in health service"
```

**Commit Types:**
- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `docs`: Documentation changes
- `refactor`: Code refactoring
- `test`: Test additions/changes
- `chore`: Maintenance tasks
- `perf`: Performance improvements
- `style`: Code style changes
- `ci`: CI/CD changes 